WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:01.424
- I've discovered a dead something

00:00:01.424 --> 00:00:02.992
in the middle of the field,

00:00:02.992 --> 00:00:04.573
and it now,

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:06.041
for the first time has become real

00:00:06.041 --> 00:00:08.379
that we're about to kill birds.

00:00:11.242 --> 00:00:12.904
More than 23 million
chickens are slaughtered

00:00:12.904 --> 00:00:13.928
in the United States...

00:00:13.928 --> 00:00:15.211
Every day.

00:00:15.211 --> 00:00:17.349
We visited a family farm to learn about

00:00:17.349 --> 00:00:19.320
poultry harvesting techniques.

00:00:22.248 --> 00:00:24.147
- We're here at Gone Straw Farms.

00:00:24.147 --> 00:00:28.514
We raise approximately
10,000 birds, give or take.

00:00:28.514 --> 00:00:31.332
You get such a great
reaction out of people

00:00:31.332 --> 00:00:35.748
after they consume something
that you spent so much effort

00:00:35.748 --> 00:00:38.212
raising and keeping safe.

00:00:38.212 --> 00:00:40.628
I hope we can enlighten some folks on

00:00:40.628 --> 00:00:43.800
the process of actually
killing your own food.

00:00:49.085 --> 00:00:49.926
- I love animals.

00:00:49.926 --> 00:00:52.058
My Instagram is all cats.

00:00:52.628 --> 00:00:55.906
- I'm not someone who
necessarily kills things.

00:00:55.906 --> 00:00:56.625
- Who knows, maybe I'll be

00:00:56.625 --> 00:00:59.137
a vegetarian tomorrow, or something.

00:01:00.461 --> 00:01:01.392
- I don't want to do this,

00:01:01.392 --> 00:01:04.169
but I think it'll be a good
educational experience.

00:01:04.169 --> 00:01:08.140
I want to know, am I okay with this?

00:01:13.747 --> 00:01:14.928
- They're huge!

00:01:14.928 --> 00:01:16.794
You want us to pick one of those up?

00:01:16.794 --> 00:01:18.810
- Um, these guys are like 10 weeks old,

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:21.545
and we do multi-age farming here.

00:01:21.545 --> 00:01:22.428
- We could...

00:01:22.428 --> 00:01:24.861
These are ones that we could kill and eat?

00:01:24.861 --> 00:01:25.593
- No, you would--

00:01:25.593 --> 00:01:27.245
I mean, if you wanted a Cornish hen,

00:01:27.245 --> 00:01:29.744
instead of 'kill,' we'll
call it 'harvest' them.

00:01:29.744 --> 00:01:30.960
- 'Harvest' feels better than...

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:33.093
- Yeah, it does, it's all part of that...

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:34.694
- Killing is something
I'd do because, like,

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:37.092
you owe me money, or
you've scorned my family,

00:01:37.092 --> 00:01:37.693
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:37.693 --> 00:01:39.878
- or I have a blood debt to settle.

00:01:39.878 --> 00:01:41.744
This is like, this is, I gotta eat.

00:01:41.744 --> 00:01:44.443
- I'll take you inside that
little plastic thing there.

00:01:44.443 --> 00:01:48.093
Those are actually five days old.

00:01:48.093 --> 00:01:50.833
Okay, these are for your shoes.

00:01:50.833 --> 00:01:51.640
- Okay.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:52.208
- Put those on.

00:01:52.208 --> 00:01:54.575
It's a little bio-security.

00:02:19.409 --> 00:02:22.568
- Chicken, hi little guy.

00:02:25.076 --> 00:02:27.209
(indistinct speech)

00:02:27.209 --> 00:02:29.768
- (laughing) Oh, look at them run around!

00:02:29.768 --> 00:02:32.480
- [man] It kinda smells
strong, like hair dye.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:35.212
- [Reese] Walk with your
feet close to the ground.

00:02:35.212 --> 00:02:38.115
They will not hurt you.

00:02:38.115 --> 00:02:39.768
- [Gabby] I have taxidermy ducklings

00:02:39.768 --> 00:02:41.701
that kinda look like this.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.311
- It feels really weird to pick something

00:02:43.311 --> 00:02:44.735
that you know you're going to kill.

00:02:44.735 --> 00:02:46.501
- It's just arbitrary,
I'm just like, yeah, you!

00:02:46.501 --> 00:02:48.103
- Alright, I'm good.

00:02:48.103 --> 00:02:48.819
- Gabby knows, Gabby knows.

00:02:48.819 --> 00:02:49.819
- Really? Ya'll are good?

00:02:49.819 --> 00:02:51.210
Like how are you good right now?

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:53.698
- Because I'm not gonna build it up!

00:02:54.883 --> 00:02:56.389
- [Reese] Really fast!

00:02:56.389 --> 00:03:01.280
- Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Ah! Sorry! Sorry!

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:05.004
- I'm sorry, little baby.

00:03:07.073 --> 00:03:09.881
- (screams) Okay, sorry.

00:03:09.881 --> 00:03:12.674
- [Gabby] Oh my God, he's so fat!

00:03:13.274 --> 00:03:15.140
- I chose a fatty.

00:03:16.432 --> 00:03:19.984
- Don't move, don't move,
okay, okay, we're okay.

00:03:19.984 --> 00:03:21.735
- We're gonna go put 'em in the cage,

00:03:21.735 --> 00:03:24.641
take 'em up to the harvest station, and

00:03:24.641 --> 00:03:26.238
do the deed.

00:03:31.334 --> 00:03:32.785
- I took my rings off,

00:03:32.785 --> 00:03:35.069
like I would for a bar fight.

00:03:35.069 --> 00:03:36.952
- This'll be the final stage for the bird,

00:03:36.952 --> 00:03:38.536
as far as him being around.

00:03:38.536 --> 00:03:41.069
We're gonna place him in
the cone, upside down.

00:03:41.069 --> 00:03:42.368
- Where my parents are
from in El Salvador,

00:03:42.368 --> 00:03:43.452
they do like the same thing,

00:03:43.452 --> 00:03:44.518
where they hang 'em upside down,

00:03:44.518 --> 00:03:45.951
and they, like, slit their throat,

00:03:45.951 --> 00:03:47.551
and that's kind of like
the way of the land,

00:03:47.551 --> 00:03:50.518
but it's still really sad.

00:03:53.947 --> 00:03:55.877
- You want to get in here, Reese?

00:03:57.231 --> 00:04:02.069
(soft chatter)

00:04:05.902 --> 00:04:06.985
- What's a shame is that,

00:04:06.985 --> 00:04:09.001
when we die, we won't
become someone's tasty meal.

00:04:09.001 --> 00:04:11.620
At least their death is
serving a greater purpose.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:13.344
- You don't want to cut through feather,

00:04:13.344 --> 00:04:15.335
but you just find a spot.

00:04:15.735 --> 00:04:16.534
You do this side,

00:04:16.534 --> 00:04:18.834
and then you do the same thing this side.

00:04:18.834 --> 00:04:20.735
You'll feel the blood rush down your hand,

00:04:20.735 --> 00:04:22.570
and that's when you know you did it right.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:24.485
- Alright, like harder, like?

00:04:24.485 --> 00:04:26.235
- About that, yeah.

00:04:26.235 --> 00:04:26.953
There, see?

00:04:26.953 --> 00:04:27.784
- [Reese] There.
- [cutter] Now what do I do?

00:04:27.784 --> 00:04:28.735
- [Reese] Let go.

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:31.115
- Ohhhhh.

00:04:33.351 --> 00:04:35.335
- [Reese] There's a hose over there.

00:04:35.335 --> 00:04:37.351
The chicken is already gone.

00:04:37.351 --> 00:04:38.952
Now as we're talking right now,

00:04:38.952 --> 00:04:40.507
she's gone.

00:04:48.209 --> 00:04:50.556
- We don't need to watch that.

00:04:56.755 --> 00:04:59.507
I feel like my response to
these kind of things is to just,

00:04:59.507 --> 00:05:01.388
to numb myself emotionally,

00:05:01.388 --> 00:05:03.729
and not really allow myself to,

00:05:04.206 --> 00:05:05.546
feel?

00:05:05.839 --> 00:05:07.713
Is that what robots say?

00:05:09.006 --> 00:05:12.255
- Ahh, that was a lot of blood.

00:05:12.255 --> 00:05:13.622
- It's so weird, the instinct to be like,

00:05:13.622 --> 00:05:14.956
it's okay, buddy, it's okay.

00:05:14.956 --> 00:05:16.694
- Umm hmm.

00:05:17.341 --> 00:05:18.856
- [Gabby] Damn, buddy.

00:05:24.598 --> 00:05:26.038
After slaughter, the feathers are loosened

00:05:26.038 --> 00:05:27.388
with hot water and
plucked with a machine...

00:05:27.388 --> 00:05:29.800
- [Reese] It's hot, keep going.

00:05:30.231 --> 00:05:32.782
Hold on to the legs,
and go all the way in.

00:05:32.782 --> 00:05:34.662
It only takes a few seconds.

00:05:37.631 --> 00:05:39.550
- Why is THIS the part I don't like?

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:41.250
- [Reese] And then when
the chicken is done,

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:42.128
you just pull the head off.

00:05:42.128 --> 00:05:44.549
- Oh my God, warning next time, warning!

00:05:44.549 --> 00:05:45.833
- Up and in.

00:05:45.833 --> 00:05:48.444
- Up and in? Ohhhh.

00:05:49.383 --> 00:05:50.565
- Gabby come help us.

00:05:50.565 --> 00:05:52.383
- Because we're city folk, we brought

00:05:52.383 --> 00:05:54.099
Trader Joe's barbecue sauce.

00:05:54.099 --> 00:05:56.231
Isn't it super weird that that was

00:05:56.231 --> 00:05:58.516
the chicken that we picked
out of the house, like

00:05:58.516 --> 00:06:00.082
a couple hours ago?

00:06:00.082 --> 00:06:01.132
- Hey, keep painting, keep painting,

00:06:01.132 --> 00:06:02.684
you're doing great.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:06.566
- [All] Oh, man, yeah.

00:06:06.566 --> 00:06:07.882
- This chicken is delicious.

00:06:07.882 --> 00:06:09.682
It tastes fresher,

00:06:09.682 --> 00:06:11.365
maybe because I saw it die.

00:06:11.365 --> 00:06:12.467
- Don't take your food for granted.

00:06:12.467 --> 00:06:16.848
Understand what it takes to harvest it,

00:06:16.848 --> 00:06:17.832
and get it on your plate.

00:06:17.832 --> 00:06:18.917
- I don't know that I'm gonna leave here

00:06:18.917 --> 00:06:21.232
vegetarian, or vegan,

00:06:21.232 --> 00:06:23.068
but I definitely am gonna

00:06:23.068 --> 00:06:26.377
think about it more.

00:06:26.854 --> 00:06:28.657
Gone Straw Farms raises
100% grass-fed chickens.

00:06:28.657 --> 00:06:30.049
Animals in this video
were raised according to

00:06:30.049 --> 00:06:31.261
global animal partnership standards.

00:06:31.261 --> 00:06:33.781
Less than 2% of slaughtered
animals in the U.S.

00:06:33.781 --> 00:06:35.550
are raised using these guidelines.

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:38.703
- Mine's so cute and
little compared to ya'll's.

00:06:40.811 --> 00:06:42.262
- It feels rude to smile during this.

00:06:42.262 --> 00:06:44.544
- I know, I'm not smiling.

